# .Renviron.example
# Copy this to .Renviron and fill in the values you need. .Renviron is
# gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# The app runs with NONE of these set: it falls back to the sibling checkout at
# ../fwise-data/ and writes submissions to ../fwise-data/inbox/.

# ---- The data repository -----------------------------------------------------
# THE VARIABLE THE DATA NEEDS. The newsletter and feedback forms need two more;
# see the last section.
#
# fwise-data is private, so an unauthenticated raw.githubusercontent.com URL
# returns 404. Set this to a fine-grained GitHub PAT - resource owner
# freshwaterLife, scoped to fwise-data, Contents: Read and write - and the app
# reads the data and writes submissions over the GitHub API.
#
# Leave it unset locally. The app then reads ../fwise-data/ and writes
# submissions to ../fwise-data/inbox/, making no network calls at all.
#
# The repository and branch are constants in R/config.R, not variables. Neither
# is a secret and neither varies.
# FWISE_DATA_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# ---- Override, not normally needed -------------------------------------------
# Wins over the token. Use it to point a test deploy at a fork, a branch or a
# local path without a code change:
#
#   /some/path   read that directory
#   https://...  read that base URL over plain HTTPS with NO credential. Cannot
#                write, so submissions will fail.
#
# Point it at the directory holding metadata.json and schema/, NOT at schema/
# itself. A trailing slash is tolerated.
#
# Setting it explicitly, as below, means the app still finds the data when run
# from a different working directory.
# FWISE_DATA_SOURCE=/absolute/path/to/fwise-data

# ---- Submissions -------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing further to configure. FWISE_DATA_TOKEN above covers both directions:
# submissions are committed to inbox/ in the same repository the data is read
# from. Without a token they are written to ../fwise-data/inbox/ instead, in the
# same one-file-per-submission shape, so the QA loop is identical.

# ---- Newsletter sign-ups and feedback ----------------------------------------
# Both forms write to one private Google Sheet, a tab each ("newsletter" and
# "feedback"), through a Google Cloud service account. BOTH variables must be
# set; with either missing the forms write to dev/forms/<tab>.csv on this
# machine instead, which is what you want locally.
#
# The sheet must be shared with the key's client_email as an Editor, and the
# Google Sheets API must be enabled in the key's Cloud project. Row 1 of each
# tab holds the column headers - see FW_NEWSLETTER_COLUMNS and
# FW_FEEDBACK_COLUMNS in R/forms_store.R - and `Rscript dev/check_sheets.R`
# checks them.
#
# The key may be the JSON itself or base64 of it. Base64 (`base64 -i key.json`)
# is one line with no quotes or newlines, so it survives a deployment console.
# FWISE_FORMS_SHEET_ID=1AbC...the id between /d/ and /edit in the sheet's URL
# GS4_SA_KEY_B64=eyJ0eXBlIjoic2VydmljZV9hY2NvdW50Ii...

# ---- Usage tracking ----------------------------------------------------------
# The in-app event log (see TRACKING.md and R/tracking.R). OFF unless
# FWISE_LOG_MODE says otherwise, so a local run never writes to the live sheet.
#
#   sheet    one row per event, appended to the `events` tab when a session
#            ends, in the forms sheet (FWISE_FORMS_SHEET_ID) unless
#            FWISE_LOG_SHEET_ID names another. Uses the forms' GS4_SA_KEY_B64.
#   console  the rows are printed to this R console instead. For testing.
#   off      nothing is recorded.
#
# Share the sheet with the key's client_email as an Editor. Row 1 of `events`
# holds: timestamp, session_id, event, detail, app_version.
# FWISE_LOG_MODE=console
# Only for a separate spreadsheet:
# FWISE_LOG_SHEET_ID=1AbC...the id between /d/ and /edit in the sheet's URL
